## N-042 — Perfection / source variant / compressed compound

**Location:** [U00707](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00707), [U00708](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00708), [U00709](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00709), [U00710](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00710), [U00711](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00711), [U00712](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00712), [U00713](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00713), [U00714](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00714), [U00715](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00715), [U00716](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00716), [U00717](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00717), [U00718](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00718), [U00719](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00719), [U00720](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00720)

**Problem and evidence:** rigs byed is compressed, and a small-print variant interrupts the capacity/transformation verse. The e-text's bus pa sbyar differs from the probable nus pa(s) sbyar reading in the scan.

**Working treatment:** Use class-formation as a literal working compound. Translate the main verse separately and identify the variant as 'applied by capacity,' with its transcription explicitly provisional. Render nye bar rdzogs as fully complete in the repeated completion sequence.

**Uncertainty:** The precise variant orthography, the force of rigs byed, and the intensive use of nye bar need approval; no unmarked source correction is made.

**Review action:** Verify the small-print variant at full resolution and approve the three local lexical decisions before polishing the repeated perfection passage.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 30.

