**Location:** [U00726](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00726), [U00727](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00727), [U00728](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00728), [U00729](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00729), [U00730](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00730), [U00731](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00731), [U00732](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00732), [U00733](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00733), [U00734](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00734), [U00735](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00735), [U00736](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00736), [U00737](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00737), [U00738](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00738), [U00739](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00739), [U00740](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00740), [U00741](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00741), [U00742](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00742), [U00743](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00743), [U00744](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00744), [U00745](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00745), [U00746](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00746), [U00747](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00747)

**Problem and evidence:** The source explains the setting through five aspects and repeatedly divides phun/gsum/tshogs into three, with different explanations for place, teacher, retinue, teaching, and time.

**Working treatment:** Retain the Tibetan component labels and translate every explanation, preserving the numbers and repetitions. Explain this as the text's interpretive wordplay, not a claim of historical etymology.

**Uncertainty:** The relation of the four gathered in time and the exact scope of the scriptural-collection phrase remain open; no unprinted collection names are added.

**Review action:** Review the five-by-three structure and the source's spelling of the middle component before adding an explanatory diagram.

