## N-044 — Ages / chronological counts

**Location:** [U00760](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00760), [U00761](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00761), [U00762](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00762), [U00763](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00763), [U00764](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00764), [U00765](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00765), [U00766](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00766), [U00774](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00774), [U00775](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00775), [U00776](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00776), [U00786](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00786), [U00787](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00787), [U00788](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00788), [U00796](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00796), [U00797](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00797), [U00798](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00798), [U00806](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00806), [U00809](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00809), [U00813](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00813), [U00836](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00836), [U00845](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00845), [U00847](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00847), [U00855](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00855), [U00860](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00860), [U00867](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00867), [U00872](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00872), [U00879](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00879), [U00883](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00883), [U00887](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00887), [U00888](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00888), [U00891](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00891), [U00897](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00897), [U00898](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00898), [U00902](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00902), [U00904](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00904), [U00905](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00905)

**Problem and evidence:** The teaching's future is described through named ages and repeated periods of flourishing and darkness. The two successive replies do not give a fully identical sequence of names and durations. Several sixty-period clauses omit the word year, and the opening explicitly speaks of ages.

**Working treatment:** Preserve every stated duration and the seven age designations without converting them to an assumed external chronology. Where years is supplied from the immediate repeated construction, put it in brackets. Retain the metaphor of the teaching's shoots.

**Uncertainty:** The relation of the two sequences and the scale of the first sixty ages remain open; the translation is the text's account, not a historical verification or an arithmetic harmonization.

**Review action:** Build a source-linked comparison of the two sequences and resolve omissions only through explicit witness evidence; do not silently equalize their counts.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 32, 33, 34, 35, 36, 37.

