## N-047 — Large numbers / temporal scale

**Location:** [U00918](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00918), [U00919](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00919), [U00920](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00920), [U00925](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00925), [U00932](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00932), [U00936](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00936), [U00938](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00938), [U00939](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00939), [U00944](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00944), [U00945](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00945), [U00946](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00946), [U00947](alignment/chapter-01.md#u00947)

**Problem and evidence:** The later transmission account uses five thousand thousands of years, the Tibetan fractional-hundred expression phyed dang brgyad, and the compressed sa ya drug 'bum count of ages.

**Working treatment:** Preserve five thousand thousands as written; render phyed dang brgyad in the usual anticipatory-half construction as seven and a half hundreds. Keep sa ya drug 'bum as the visibly unresolved numerical phrase 'a million, six hundred thousand,' without asserting an addition or multiplication.

**Uncertainty:** The arithmetic grouping at U00944 remains unresolved. No numeric conversion table or universal chronology is supplied as though established.

**Review action:** Confirm the grouping from the selected witness and approved numerical usage before replacing the literal phrase with an Arabic numeral.

