**Location:** [U01336](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01336), [U01337](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01337), [U01338](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01338), [U01339](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01339), [U01340](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01340), [U01341](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01341), [U01342](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01342), [U01343](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01343), [U01344](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01344), [U01345](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01345), [U01346](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01346), [U01347](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01347), [U01348](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01348), [U01349](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01349), [U01350](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01350), [U01351](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01351), [U01352](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01352)

**Problem and evidence:** The text states sixty excellences and three sets of twelve deeds, then gives the qualities of those to be trained in relation to the teacher's arrival. The outer/inner/secret relation to four activities is compressed. gzhi ma concerns the teaching's foundation.

**Working treatment:** Retain the explicit counts without enumerating unlisted members. Preserve embodiment, speech and awakened mind as distinct. Use foundation as a recorded contextual proposal for gzhi ma, not as a replacement for the technical Ground elsewhere.

**Uncertainty:** Whether the qualities belong to the recipients or are benefits for them, and how the three scopes modify the four activities, need review.

**Review action:** Confirm these attachments and compare the three sets with the earlier thirty-six-deed statement without importing a conventional list.

