gnment/chapter-01.md#u01902), [U01903](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01903), [U01904](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01904), [U01905](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01905)

**Problem and evidence:** ngo che and ngo mi chogs frame the teaching through regard and inability to refuse. The mental-faculty-of-samsara clause, desired qualities, the two named embodiments, and freedom from sound before empowerment are compressed. The text explicitly describes cutting outer and inner breath flow.

**Working treatment:** Keep the relationship wording provisional, bracket the supplied orientation of mental faculty, retain only the two named embodiments, and do not replace freedom from sound with mastery of sound. Preserve the breath statement as source content with a visibly editorial instruction not to attempt breath cessation from this draft. Maintain meditative stabilization distinct from deep absorption.

**Uncertainty:** Several clause attachments and the fifth neuter-empty referent remain unsettled. The text's liberation, lifespan and breath claims are not independently validated or approved as practical instructions.

**Review action:** Review the complete sensory-practice sequence and terminology before use; do not undertake hazardous breath restriction on the basis of this translation.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 72, 73, 74.

