## N-086 — Entity/empty transferring / referents / source spelling

**Location:** [U01907](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01907), [U01908](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01908), [U01909](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01909), [U01910](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01910), [U01911](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01911), [U01912](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01912), [U01913](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01913), [U01914](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01914), [U01915](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01915), [U01916](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01916), [U01917](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01917), [U01918](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01918), [U01919](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01919), [U01920](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01920), [U01921](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01921), [U01922](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01922), [U01923](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01923), [U01924](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01924), [U01925](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01925), [U01926](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01926), [U01927](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01927), [U01928](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01928), [U01929](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01929), [U01930](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01930), [U01931](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01931), [U01932](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01932), [U01933](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01933), [U01934](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01934), [U01935](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01935), [U01936](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01936)

**Problem and evidence:** The account distinguishes transferring into entities from emptiness. Its release/voice clause and invisible-form/all-bodies result are compressed. gzhon pa'i gzugs at U01932 gives a youthful-form reading, not an established mount reading. The source restricts taking material things to offerings for the guru.

**Working treatment:** Keep both types and every restriction, preserve basic space and dharma embodiment as distinct, and leave the youthful-form reading queried rather than silently changing gzhon to bzhon. Do not reconstruct an occult technique or endorse taking others' property. Apply the U01921–U01922 alignment correction.

**Uncertainty:** The material-object referent, invisible form, youthful forms and entering ordinary mind require review. Transferring here is not automatically the same scope as the preceding spiritual transference category.

**Review action:** Resolve the lexical and grammatical questions from the source; retain the described acts as historical religious claims, not recommendations.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 74, 75.

