**Location:** [U01938](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01938), [U01939](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01939), [U01940](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01940), [U01941](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01941), [U01942](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01942), [U01943](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01943), [U01944](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01944), [U01945](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01945), [U01946](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01946), [U01947](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01947), [U01948](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01948), [U01949](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01949), [U01950](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01950), [U01951](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01951), [U01952](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01952), [U01953](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01953), [U01954](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01954), [U01955](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01955), [U01956](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01956), [U01957](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01957), [U01958](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01958), [U01959](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01959), [U01960](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01960), [U01961](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01961), [U01962](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01962), [U01963](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01963), [U01964](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01964), [U01965](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01965), [U01966](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01966), [U01967](alignment/chapter-01.md#u01967)

**Problem and evidence:** rigs bcas sems kyi bsdus at U01939 leaves its attachment unclear. The source claims illness can be transferred to living beings and describes insentient supports and a series of operations; it later prohibits the efficacy of taking for personal worldly desire.

**Working treatment:** Preserve the unclear family/ordinary-mind construction, every support and operation, and the final negative condition. Bracket illness as the supplied object of release where implicit. Do not add an operational mechanism, claim that disease can actually be transferred by this method, or recommend harming others or appropriating property.

**Uncertainty:** The family referent, the status of the listed signs, and the scope of the actual-release predicate remain provisional. No clinical or empirical verification has been performed.

**Review action:** Review the complete sequence and its limiting conditions philologically; do not apply the described acts as treatment or instructions for conduct.

