<a id="n-091"></a>

## N-091 — Five culminations / compound boundaries / terminology proposals

**Location:** [U02022](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02022), [U02023](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02023), [U02024](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02024), [U02025](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02025), [U02026](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02026), [U02027](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02027), [U02028](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02028), [U02029](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02029), [U02030](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02030), [U02031](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02031), [U02032](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02032), [U02033](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02033), [U02034](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02034), [U02035](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02035), [U02036](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02036), [U02037](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02037), [U02038](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02038), [U02039](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02039), [U02040](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02040), [U02041](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02041), [U02042](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02042), [U02043](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02043), [U02044](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02044), [U02045](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02045)

**Problem and evidence:** Generation, completion, tenets, Mahamudra and Great Perfection have distinct union and culmination statements. yid la byed pa and cog bzhag lack whole-expression entries. rang bzhin rdzogs pa chen po and snang shes chos nyid permit more than one attachment. Five subsequent results may summarize the preceding five, but the correspondence is not explicitly labeled.

**Working treatment:** Preserve every stage, union and result in order; retain canonical Mahamudra, intrinsic nature, primordial liberation, conceptual mind and mental faculty. Provisionally render mental engagement and leaving just as it is. Do not replace the appearance/knowing/nature-of-phenomena wording with a generic nonduality formula.

**Uncertainty:** The stage boundaries, the syntax of the two Great Perfection compounds and the mapping of the final five statements remain provisional.

**Review action:** Approve the whole-expression proposals and review the connected sequence without importing an external graded practice scheme.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 79, 80.

