**Problem and evidence:** Yoginī, the Ray-Bearing One and tsan ti ka have seven, three and three practices. The source describes letter combinations but does not print complete mantras or specify colors and forms. phyi nas at U02061 could be spatial or verbal. The sealing/restoring statements are compressed. Several numerical sequences lack an explicit counting unit.

**Working treatment:** Keep methods distinct from discerning knowing and preserve all numbers without adding repetitions, days or multipliers. Use descriptive/source-syllabic deity designations rather than externally identifying a specific form. Retain āli, kāli and clarifiers, bracket supplied referents, and leave from outside provisional. Do not reconstruct missing mantras, iconography or ritual instructions.

**Uncertainty:** Name identities, the phyi verb/preposition issue, the sealing/restoration construction and the units of the counts remain unresolved. Accomplishment claims are those of the source.

**Review action:** Review the complete ritual clauses and approve the name/term concordance; identify missing specifications only from authorized evidence.

