<a id="n-101"></a>

## N-101 — Pledges/vows / absent heading / aspirational ground

**Location:** [U02300](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02300), [U02301](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02301), [U02302](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02302), [U02303](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02303), [U02304](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02304), [U02305](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02305), [U02306](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02306), [U02307](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02307), [U02308](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02308), [U02309](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02309), [U02310](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02310), [U02311](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02311), [U02312](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02312), [U02313](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02313), [U02314](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02314), [U02315](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02315), [U02316](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02316), [U02317](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02317), [U02318](alignment/chapter-01.md#u02318)

**Problem and evidence:** The pledge account distinguishes embodiment/speech/awakened mind from the yogin's body/speech/mental faculty. It is followed by a discussion of words and nine stages without an explicit fifty-seventh-reply heading; the next printed heading is fifty-eighth. mos pa spyod pa'i sa is a whole technical expression absent from the glossary.

**Working treatment:** Preserve the two triads, guru and vajra-sibling objects, and the difference between pledges and vows. Do not invent the missing numbered heading. Provisionally render the full stage expression as ground of aspirational activity, with lower-case ground representing sa rather than gzhi. The source's prediction about future adherents is translated, not independently asserted.

**Uncertainty:** The exact transition between replies fifty-six and fifty-seven, the referent of the final teaching period and the stage designation remain open.

**Review action:** Review the transition with the corresponding questions and retain the heading gap explicitly in the structural record.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 89, 90.

