## N-125 — Bodily primordial knowing / citta / fivefold groups / difficult relation

**Location:** [U02858](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02858), [U02859](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02859), [U02860](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02860), [U02861](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02861), [U02862](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02862), [U02863](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02863), [U02864](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02864), [U02865](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02865), [U02866](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02866), [U02867](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02867), [U02868](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02868), [U02869](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02869), [U02870](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02870), [U02871](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02871), [U02872](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02872), [U02873](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02873), [U02874](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02874), [U02875](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02875), [U02876](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02876), [U02877](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02877), [U02878](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02878), [U02879](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02879), [U02880](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02880), [U02881](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02881), [U02882](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02882), [U02883](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02883), [U02884](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02884), [U02885](alignment/chapter-02.md#u02885)

**Problem and evidence:** The body/embodiment/radiance sequence is compressed. Four and two portions are mentioned before fivefold groups. citta is a Sanskrit-derived designation in a bodily-channel context; the eight-corner/door wording does not explicitly count eight doors separately. The final joining-to-delusion arrangement is difficult.

**Working treatment:** Propose heart for citta while retaining the source term and documenting the bodily-context inference. Preserve all counts without harmonizing them, keep radiance distinct from splendor, and leave the U02884 relation provisional. Do not replace the symbolic bodily account with modern anatomical claims.

**Uncertainty:** The precise citta referent, the eight-corner/door attachment, the four/two grouping and the delusion-arrangement clause remain open.

**Review action:** Approve the contextual citta proposal and review the full body-to-vision account against the source gloss and subsequent channel discussion.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 110, 111.

