## N-133 — Paired embodiments / hero designation / srang and 'dun queries

**Location:** [U03041](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03041), [U03042](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03042), [U03043](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03043), [U03044](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03044), [U03045](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03045), [U03046](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03046), [U03047](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03047), [U03048](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03048), [U03049](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03049), [U03050](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03050), [U03051](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03051), [U03052](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03052), [U03053](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03053), [U03054](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03054), [U03055](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03055)

**Problem and evidence:** The source explicitly gives two embodiments from paired portions. khyab bdag sems dpa' is not externally identified. srang can bear different senses, and the vajra-chain phrase does not settle its referent. 'dun pa at U03050 is difficult in relation to embodiments and spheres.

**Working treatment:** Preserve two rather than normalize to three, translate the hero designation descriptively, and retain balance (srang) as a queried rendering. Use aspiration provisionally for 'dun pa. Keep the later exhaustion of the three embodiments and the full apprehended-object/apprehending-subject pair intact.

**Uncertainty:** The hero's identity, srang, the aspiration/convergence relation and the implied subject of several predicates remain unresolved.

**Review action:** Compare these expressions with U03125–U03129 and other explicit occurrences before approving a consistent contextual interpretation.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 117.

