## N-136 — Elemental pairings / explicit source query / mental faculties and bodily terms

**Location:** [U03135](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03135), [U03136](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03136), [U03137](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03137), [U03138](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03138), [U03139](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03139), [U03140](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03140), [U03141](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03141), [U03142](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03142), [U03143](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03143), [U03144](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03144), [U03145](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03145), [U03146](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03146), [U03147](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03147), [U03148](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03148), [U03149](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03149), [U03150](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03150), [U03151](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03151), [U03152](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03152), [U03153](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03153), [U03154](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03154), [U03155](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03155), [U03156](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03156), [U03157](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03157), [U03158](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03158), [U03159](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03159), [U03160](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03160), [U03161](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03161), [U03162](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03162), [U03163](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03163), [U03164](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03164), [U03165](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03165), [U03166](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03166), [U03167](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03167)

**Problem and evidence:** The source alternates genitive and instrumental-looking particles in the elemental pairings. It expressly notes that water's wind occurs twice. Several effects are compressed: strong inclination/little perception, supreme or pure faculties, alternating interruptions, and joints/limbs in a largely mental-faculty account.

**Working treatment:** Preserve the written sequence, both water/wind occurrences and the source's query. Treat the paired-element possessive wording as a provisional construction, not an asserted causal matrix. Retain perception as the active 'du shes entry, preserve joints/limbs rather than replace them with verbal parts, and bracket the repeated fire/wind group labels where omitted.

**Uncertainty:** The case relationships, the duplicate's intended correction, several predicates and the scope of dag at U03155 remain unsettled. No empirical assessment of intelligence, personality or faculties is made.

**Review action:** Collate the pairings without forcing a four-by-four table, and review all proposed grammatical supplements against the source.

