**Problem and evidence:** The source combines bodily effects, lamps, practices and particle designations. don dam byang sems extends the earlier unresolved short expression into a new context. Sheep/ox particles and sun particles may be technical size terms, but the source does not spell out hair tips or measurement ratios.

**Working treatment:** Preserve all four elements, their separate effects and lamp relations. Record the new contextual use of awakening ordinary mind as provisional, retain the particle names without adding an unstated measurement system, and keep differentiating conceptualization distinct from ordinary mind. The bodily and aging claims remain claims of the translated source.

**Uncertainty:** The byang sems sense, particle designations, the wind-refined-part construction and final time/method syntax remain unresolved. No medical or nutritional efficacy is established.

**Review action:** Review the technical terms against authorized evidence; do not treat this draft as a treatment or nourishment protocol.

