## N-150 — Packing the lamp / unspecified supports / three appearances / editorial safety

**Location:** [U03433](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03433), [U03434](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03434), [U03435](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03435), [U03436](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03436), [U03437](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03437), [U03438](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03438), [U03439](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03439), [U03440](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03440), [U03441](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03441), [U03442](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03442), [U03443](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03443), [U03444](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03444), [U03445](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03445), [U03446](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03446), [U03447](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03447), [U03448](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03448), [U03449](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03449), [U03450](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03450), [U03451](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03451), [U03452](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03452), [U03453](alignment/chapter-02.md#u03453)

**Problem and evidence:** The source names three supports without listing them and mentions thumb and forefinger without a complete procedure. It first names the direct-perception vision, then experience and two further appearance phrases, finally saying three appearances. These are not textually identical to the established four-vision list.

**Working treatment:** Retain the unspecified three, the body-part reference and the canonical direct-perception vision. Preserve the subsequent appearance names and the written threefold total without forcing a four-vision mapping. Distinguish the editorial warning against inferred eye pressure from the source's words.

**Uncertainty:** The supports, physical application and exact grouping of the three appearances require review. This is not a safe, complete or authorized practical instruction.

**Review action:** Obtain source-based clarification of the procedure and categories; do not infer or perform pressure on the eyes or related manipulations from this draft.

