## N-169 — Karma/faculties / source bral / three-nine-twenty-one calculation

**Location:** [U03898](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03898), [U03899](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03899), [U03900](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03900), [U03901](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03901), [U03902](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03902), [U03903](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03903), [U03904](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03904), [U03905](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03905), [U03906](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03906), [U03907](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03907), [U03908](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03908), [U03909](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03909), [U03910](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03910), [U03911](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03911), [U03912](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03912), [U03913](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03913), [U03914](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03914), [U03915](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03915), [U03916](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03916), [U03917](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03917), [U03918](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03918), [U03919](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03919), [U03920](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03920), [U03921](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03921), [U03922](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03922), [U03923](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03923), [U03924](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03924), [U03925](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03925), [U03926](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03926), [U03927](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03927), [U03928](alignment/chapter-03.md#u03928)

**Problem and evidence:** The seven-point introduction includes three, nine and twenty-one. U03922 reads 'du shes bral, free from perception, rather than an assumed differentiation verb. The later division into nine, two sets of nine and three placed in the Ground is explicit but its ontological scope is not defined.

**Working treatment:** Preserve the cloud/wind simile and all numerical operations actually stated. Retain the active perception mapping and the written bral with a query rather than silently change it to dbye. Keep taking up and experiencing as activities, not a claim of contemporary causal validation.

**Uncertainty:** The seven-point grouping, free-from-perception statement, relation of Ground to the added three and the meaning of appearances in the count require review.

**Review action:** Collate U03922 and review the full count sequence without inventing vehicle subcategories or a psychological model.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 149, 150.

