## N-175 — Enlightened intent / foundation construction

**Location:** [U04015](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04015), [U04016](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04016), [U04017](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04017), [U04018](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04018), [U04019](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04019), [U04020](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04020), [U04021](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04021), [U04022](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04022), [U04023](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04023), [U04024](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04024), [U04025](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04025), [U04026](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04026), [U04027](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04027), [U04028](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04028), [U04029](alignment/chapter-03.md#u04029)

**Problem and evidence:** The source uses the honorific dgongs verbally with cir mi and describes gzhi ma before the explicit gzhi designation. The causation expressed by med phyir snang and snang phyir stong must not be weakened to a mere list.

**Working treatment:** Retain enlightened intent in the verb construction, use foundation provisionally for gzhi ma, and preserve the two because clauses. The later explicitly named Ground retains its established term.

**Uncertainty:** The subject and scope of cir mi dgongs and whether gzhi ma is the technical Ground remain open; the causal particles themselves are explicit.

**Review action:** Approve the construction-level use without changing dgongs pa or gzhi globally.

