## N-199 — Recognition sequence / etiology of names / alignment

**Location:** [U04660](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04660), [U04661](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04661), [U04662](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04662), [U04663](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04663), [U04664](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04664), [U04665](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04665), [U04666](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04666), [U04667](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04667), [U04668](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04668), [U04669](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04669), [U04670](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04670), [U04671](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04671), [U04672](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04672), [U04673](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04673), [U04674](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04674), [U04675](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04675), [U04676](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04676), [U04677](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04677), [U04678](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04678), [U04679](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04679), [U04680](alignment/chapter-04.md#u04680)

**Problem and evidence:** The compressed ngo/shes/grol/mthong sequence precedes three certainties. The phrase gsal gdab has a clarification/reminder range. The final predicate explicitly says the continuum ceases.

**Working treatment:** Keep identity, knowing, seeing, recognition, trust and confidence distinct in the working syntax; render making clear provisionally. Preserve continuum ceases. An initial output alignment error in U04661–U04720 was repaired before assembly, with the pre-repair file retained outside the repository.

**Uncertainty:** Exact grouping in U04665–U04670 and the technical force of the continuum's cessation remain open; corrected indexing does not settle these meanings.

**Review action:** Review the complete three-certainty construction and confirm that each corrected English line follows its exact source unit.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 175, 176.

