**Location:** [U05001](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05001), [U05002](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05002), [U05003](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05003), [U05004](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05004), [U05005](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05005), [U05006](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05006), [U05007](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05007), [U05008](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05008), [U05009](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05009), [U05010](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05010), [U05011](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05011), [U05012](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05012), [U05013](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05013), [U05014](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05014), [U05015](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05015), [U05016](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05016), [U05017](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05017), [U05018](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05018), [U05019](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05019), [U05020](alignment/chapter-05.md#u05020)

**Problem and evidence:** This continues U04998's paradoxical life-cutting statement. Dharma leads to lower destinies, cultivating gathers afflictions, and a person expounds scripture while taking another's life. The passage explicitly introduces symbolic meaning and closes its examples with ya re cha. The la construction at U05002 is difficult.

**Working treatment:** Preserve the reversals and mark supplied predicates in brackets. Translate ya re cha as How strange without endorsing the acts or inventing an unprinted allegorical key. Keep the hell/king-of-Dharma relation provisionally locative.

**Uncertainty:** The symbolic referents and U05001–U05003 attachment remain unresolved; these are not operational instructions or ethical permissions supplied by the translator.

**Review action:** Interpret only with the full chapter and source-based commentary, especially the explicit conduct and pledge requirements at U05039–U05062.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 187, 188.

