<a id="n-238"></a>

## N-238 — Final catalogue-like note / seven mother-and-child texts

**Location:** [U05465](alignment/closing-material.md#u05465), [U05466](alignment/closing-material.md#u05466)

**Problem and evidence:** The final line says the Thal Gyur continuum has ma bu bdun, seven mother-and-child, without supplying a list or explicitly repeating texts.

**Working treatment:** Preserve seven and mother-and-child, with texts in brackets, followed by all three virtue formulas. Do not invent seven titles or identify this with the earlier sixteen/seventeen list automatically.

**Uncertainty:** The set's identity and scope remain unresolved; it may be a textual-family note rather than part of the preceding invocation.

**Review action:** Establish the seven-member referent from source-based catalogue or commentary evidence before adding a list.

**Saved associated scan pages (mapping unverified):** 205.

<details>
<summary>Exact Tibetan at the recorded source units</summary>

